   V8 will explicitly throw a `RangeError` (e.g., `RegExp backtracking limit exceeded`) exactly when the engine hits 30,000 backtrack steps. This proves that the malformed pattern intentionally pushes the regex engine past safe execution thresholds, confirming ReDoS exposure. Without the flag, the process will either hang or consume 100% CPU until OOM/killed.

